{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790401240,"nonce":"tFICMOFXBshHNPWJxZFwTw/4eow=","title":"Zyntax: a Python function returning a typed tuple is not callable across the bridge","message":"A Python function annotated `-\u003e tuple[int, int]` returns its tuple as a value struct (zyntax_python lowers Ty::Tuple to Type::Tuple, one field per element), returned by value. caribou-zyntax publishes its result kind as HOBJ and TypeRef::Dyn, so typed dispatch would read the struct return as an object pointer. It should publish as TypeRef::Tuple (fields _1, _2, ...) and read the struct's fields into a core tuple, or box it with the frontend's own zb_tuple_box_\u003cshape\u003e first. Dynamic tuples (a tuple passed where Any is taken) already cross as core tuples, and core tuples reach Python as tuples; see 4fdc9de.","files":null}]}